  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chad - Flood</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to weeks of torrential rains starting in July 2024, Chad faces catastrophic floods, surpassing previous flood events in scale and impact. Over 1.9 million people have been affected, with substantial losses in life, homes, and livelihoods. The floods have created urgent needs for food, shelter, health services, water, sanitation, hygiene, and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Emergency Appeal focuses on assisting populations affected by severe flooding in Chad. It includes an operational strategy to support immediate humanitarian needs and foster resilience in the longer term.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC), in coordination with the Chadian Red Cross, aims to provide a multi-sectoral response. The appeal seeks CHF 8 million to implement emergency relief efforts, including food aid, temporary shelters, health support, and WASH interventions, while also building long-term resilience through community engagement, disaster risk reduction, and training.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary intervention areas cover eight flood-affected provinces in Chad, with a focus on regions severely impacted by the floods and those with limited resources for recovery and resilience efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The response targets 389,000 of the most vulnerable individuals affected by the floods, prioritizing women, children, elderly persons, people with disabilities, and other at-risk groups across Chad.</narrative>
  </description>
